CORE
main.py
--unwind 6
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
A function calling a constructor-returning function defined LATER in the file
bound the call result as an object struct, while the callee returned a
pointer to a fresh object (the return type was only fixed when the callee's
body was converted), so the field read was garbage. Signatures now get the
reference-instance return rules when they are registered, and freshness is
computed for every function before any body is converted.
